{"ts": 1794793477.27, "kind": "tool", "tool": "search_knowledge", "args": {"query": "Interlagos Brazil track characteristics uphill straight infield energy recovery", "k": 4}, "latency_s": 0.04, "result": {"query": "Interlagos Brazil track characteristics uphill straight infield energy recovery", "passages": [{"source": "OPTIMAL LAP SCRIPTS/docs/2026-07-15-prefp1-universal-calibration-design.md", "heading": "2. Insight", "text": "The transfer has three parts:\n- **Corner-speed ratio `r(v25) = v26/v25`** at matched corner minima. Physically: low-speed\n  corners are mechanical-grip dominated (r \u2248 1.0), high-speed corners are downforce dominated\n  (r \u2248 0.85 with \u2248\u221230% DF). Fit piecewise-linear in v25, constrained monotone non-increasing.\n  Quali pairs anchor the fit; FP1 pairs are shape-validation only (non-push laps).\n- **Top-speed / drag mapping with per-track air density.** \u03c1 from altitude (ISA model).\n  Austria's 680 m elevation explains most of the 0.60-vs-0.80 CDA gap; Mexico (2240 m) makes\n  \u03c1(altitude) mandatory later this season regardless. Residual after \u03c1-correction = wing level,\n  mapped from the track's 2025 effective drag (derived from its 2025 top-speed/power balance).\n- **Lap-delta band** `(T26\u2212T25)/T25` from Q\u2013Q pairs (observed \u2248 +1.7\u2026+2.4%) \u2192 per-track gate\n  band, replacing hardcoded seconds.", "score": 0.715}, {"source": "OPTIMAL LAP SCRIPTS/GT3/portimao/gt3_car_notes.md", "heading": "Track", "text": "## Track\n- SVG: Portimao_GP.svg = Commons \"Autodromo do Algarve alt.svg\" (identical geometry to \"... F1 Sectors.svg\").\n  Procrustes vs real 2021 F1 Q telemetry (FastF1, HAM): 8.0 m rms, not mirrored (other SVG: 11.0 m, different final corners).\n- 4653 m, road width 13.0 m (pipeline default; NOT verified), min radius 9 m. Engine drives the real (clockwise) direction.\n- Real S/F is 162 m before the sim's index 0 -> roll before render (GT3/portimao/_sf_check.py).\n- Elevation (29 m span in 2021 FastF1 Z) NOT modelled in the sim (engine is flat).", "score": 0.692}, {"source": "OPTIMAL LAP SCRIPTS/GT3/portimao/gt3_car_notes.md", "heading": "v2 (2026-10-14) - REPLACES v1 (user rejected v1: line from my pattern search + apex penalty, car fitted to a lap time)", "text": "## v2 (2026-10-14) - REPLACES v1 (user rejected v1: line from my pattern search + apex penalty, car fitted to a lap time)\nSource: real AMG GT3 Evo onboard, Portimao trackday 2021 (YouTube WT6IaGKG9Ic, Race Navigator overlay), ~1:43.0.\nSpeed OCR + lateral g -> real_amg_gt3_trackday.json; kinematic accel = dv/dt (slope removed with 2021 FastF1 z).\nCAR = measured envelope only (gt3_car_measured.json):\n- power/drag: least squares on 4 sustained full-throttle runs -> 319 kW, CdA 1.09 (resid 0.04 g). (p95 binning gave\n  324 kW / 0.78 -> 276 km/h top; dv/dt noise inflates percentiles - don't use percentiles for power.)\n- lateral: g_lat at the 7 corner apices -> mu_lat 1.67, cl 0.39 (readout quantised 0.1 g; slow corners only).\n- braking: decel p95 per bin 60-180 km/h -> mu_long 1.42, trail_v 135, trail_min 0.10, trail_exp 0.86. traction 0.85 g.\nHILLS: sim_gt3_car.simulate(elev=True default) add", "score": 0.689}, {"source": "OPTIMAL LAP SCRIPTS/GT3/portimao/gt3_car_notes.md", "heading": "Reference lap", "text": "## Reference lap\n- International GT Open 2025 Portimao Q (27 Apr 2025, racingsportscars.com): pole 1:39.966 Porsche 992 GT3 R;\n  best Mercedes-AMG GT3 Evo 1:40.051 (#9 GetSpeed, Bartone/Schiller). TARGET = 100.051 s.\n  Caveat: GT Open BoP/tyres differ from GTWC (SRO BoP, Pirelli). Friday GTWC times will re-anchor.", "score": 0.686}], "withheld": 0, "note": null}}
